# The pre-push gate is executed by `sh`, and `core.autocrlf=true` on this
# machine would hand a fresh clone a script with CRLF line endings. A shell
# refusing its own shebang is a guard that is silently absent — the shape
# invariant 7 exists for — so the one file whose LINE ENDINGS are load-bearing
# says so here rather than depending on whoever clones it next.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
